⍝ lib/complex.imo — spec notation — trusted prelude, part 14: functions of a complex variable: elementary functions with principal branches, special functions, constants
⍝ Every function returns a lazy number with a modulus of convergence: element n is within 2⁻ⁿ of the value (|error| in ℂ),
⍝ unless its description says otherwise.  Internally a number to be computed is a "regular stream" (element m within 2⁻ᵐ);
⍝ approximants are exact ℚ[i] fractions kept short by truncation (below).  Branch cuts and principal values follow C99 / Python's
⍝ cmath (a point on a cut gets the value of +0 imaginary part); at a pole, and for log 0, the value is 0.
⍝ ---- digit strings as rulers: list lengths stand for numbers, so precision bookkeeping needs no arithmetic
⍝ (dropl ρ ξ) drops as many elements from ξ as ρ has;  (le ξ η) is length ξ ≤ length η;  (excess ξ η) is ξ without its first
⍝ length-η elements (empty if ξ is not longer)
dropl_cx ∶ 𝔏 α → 𝔏 β → 𝔏 β
dropl_cx ρ ξ ≔ (ρ (θ ι ↦ (dropl_cx ι (⌄ ξ))) ξ)
le_cx ∶ 𝔏 α → 𝔏 β → 𝔹
le_cx ξ η ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (η (θ′ ι′ ↦ (le_cx ι ι′)) ⊥)) ⊤)
excess_cx ∶ 𝔏 α → 𝔏 β → 𝔏 α
excess_cx ξ η ≔ (η (θ ι ↦ (excess_cx (⌄ ξ) ι)) ξ)
ruler_cx ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 𝔹
ruler_cx ν ≔ (unary_cx (↓ᶻ ν))
⍝ a natural number (digit string) as a ruler, by halving: n = 2k or 2k + 1 (even ⇔ last digit 0 for a real integer)
unary_cx ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔹
unary_cx ξ ≔ ((∅ᶻ ξ) ⊥ ((⌃ ξ) (∷ ⊥ ((θ ↦ (⧺ θ θ)) (unary_cx (½ᶻ (⊟ᶻ ξ (◀ 1)))))) ((θ ↦ (⧺ θ θ)) (unary_cx (½ᶻ ξ)))))
⍝ a ruler of 2m + c elements
rul2_cx ∶ ℕ → ℕ → 𝔏 𝔹
rul2_cx μ ν ≔ (ruler_cx (⊞ (⊠ 1100 μ) ν))
⍝ ---- magnitudes from the top digits.  For a canonical digit string z of length L, magp z = (lo, hi) (lengths of two lists) with
⍝ 2^lo ≤ |z|² ≤ 2^hi: with t the top min(L, 16) digits, n = |t|² and 2^(j−1) ≤ n < 2ʲ, z = t·b^d + r (d = L − 16, |r| < 2.415·2^(d/2),
⍝ |t| ≥ 25.2 for 16 canonical digits) gives 2^(d+j−2) ≤ |z|² ≤ 2^(d+j+1); for L ≤ 16, 2^(j−1) ≤ |z|² < 2ʲ.  (lo, hi) = (0, 0) for z = 0.
blz_cx ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹
blz_cx ν π λ ≔ ((⩾ᶻ ν π) (blz_cx ν (⊞ᶻ π π) (∷ ⊥ λ)) λ)
⍝ the top 16 digits as a ruler
rsix_cx ∶ 𝔏 𝔹
rsix_cx ≔ (ruler_cx 100000000)
magp_cx ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔓 (𝔏 𝔹) (𝔏 𝔹)
magp_cx ζ ≔ ((∅ ζ) (⊗ ⊥ ⊥) ((δ ↦ ((τ ↦ ((ν ↦ ((∅ δ) (⊗ (⌄ ν) ν) (⊗ (⧺ δ (⌄ (⌄ ν))) (⧺ δ (∷ ⊥ ν))))) (blz_cx (⊠ᶻ τ (∗ᶻ τ)) (◀ 1) ⊥))) (dropl_cx δ ζ))) (dropl_cx rsix_cx ζ)))
⍝ the cheap bounds used by the truncations: a canonical string of length L has 0.0958·2^(L/2) ≤ |z| < 2.415·2^(L/2), so
⍝ 2^(L−7) ≤ |z|² ≤ 2^(L+3) (and |z|² ≥ 1 for z ≠ 0): mag z = (L − 7, L + 3) as rulers, without arithmetic
mag_cx ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔓 (𝔏 𝔹) (𝔏 𝔹)
mag_cx ζ ≔ ((∅ ζ) (⊗ ⊥ ⊥) (⊗ (⌄⁴ (⌄ (⌄ (⌄ ζ)))) (∷ ⊥ (∷ ⊥ (∷ ⊥ ζ)))))
⍝ ---- truncation.  For x = p/q (canonical digit strings) dropping the s lowest digits of p and of q gives x′ = p′/q′ with
⍝ |x − x′| ≤ 2⁻ᵐ when s ≤ lq − 2·max(m, 2) − 5 − max(0, hp − lq)  (2^lq ≤ |q|², |p|² ≤ 2^hp).  Proof: with p = p′bˢ + r₁, q = q′bˢ + r₂
⍝ (|rᵢ| < 2.415·2^(s/2)), x − x′ = (r₁ − x′r₂)/q, so |x − x′| ≤ 1.12·2.415·2^(s/2)·(1 + |x|)/|q| ≤ 2^(2.44 + (s − lq + max(0, hp − lq))/2).
⍝ A real denominator stays real: then s is a multiple of 4 (b⁴ = −4 is real) and the real parts of p′, q′ are kept (q = Re(q′)bˢ + Re r₂
⍝ with |Re r₂| ≤ |r₂|: the same bound), so real numbers keep real numerators and denominators.  The ruler holds 2·max(m, 2) + 5 elements.
dropn_cx ∶ 𝔏 α → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔓 𝔇 𝔇
dropn_cx σ ξ η ≔ (σ (θ ι ↦ (dropn_cx ι (⌄ ξ) (⌄ η))) (⊗ ξ η))
dropn4_cx ∶ 𝔏 α → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔓 𝔇 𝔇
dropn4_cx σ ξ η ≔ ((∅ (⌄ (⌄ (⌄ σ)))) (⊗ ξ η) (dropn4_cx (⌄⁴ σ) (⌄⁴ ξ) (⌄⁴ η)))
trp_cx ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → ℚ[i]
trp_cx ρ ξ η ≔ ((σ ↦ ((realᶻ η) ((π′ ↦ (⊗ ((realᶻ ξ) (ℜᶻ (◀ π′)) (◀ π′)) (ℜᶻ (▶ π′)))) (dropn4_cx σ ξ η)) (dropn_cx σ ξ η))) ((λ ↦ (dropl_cx (⧺ ρ (excess_cx (▶ (mag_cx ξ)) λ)) λ)) (◀ (mag_cx η))))
tr_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℕ → ℚ[i]
tr_cx ξ μ ≔ (trp_cx (rul2_cx (max μ 1100) 111010001) (⊡ (◀ ξ)) (⊡ (▶ ξ)))
⍝ joint truncation of two fractions σ/ζ, τ/ζ with one denominator (hp the larger of the two numerators), passed on to a continuation κ σ′ τ′ ζ′
dropj_cx ∶ 𝔏 α → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → (𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → β) → β
dropj_cx ρ σ τ ζ κ ≔ (ρ (θ ι ↦ (dropj_cx ι (⌄ σ) (⌄ τ) (⌄ ζ) κ)) (κ σ τ ζ))
dropj4_cx ∶ 𝔏 α → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → (𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → β) → β
dropj4_cx ρ σ τ ζ κ ≔ ((∅ (⌄ (⌄ (⌄ ρ)))) (κ σ τ (ℜᶻ ζ)) (dropj4_cx (⌄⁴ ρ) (⌄⁴ σ) (⌄⁴ τ) (⌄⁴ ζ) κ))
trj_cx ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → (𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → β) → β
trj_cx ρ σ τ ζ κ ≔ ((σ′ τ′ ζ′ ↦ ((ω ↦ ((realᶻ ζ′) (dropj4_cx ω σ′ τ′ ζ′ (σ″ τ″ ζ″ ↦ (κ ((realᶻ σ′) (ℜᶻ σ″) σ″) ((realᶻ τ′) (ℜᶻ τ″) τ″) ζ″))) (dropj_cx ω σ′ τ′ ζ′ κ))) ((λ υ₁ υ₂ ↦ (dropl_cx (⧺ ρ (excess_cx ((le_cx υ₁ υ₂) υ₂ υ₁) λ)) λ)) (◀ (mag_cx ζ′)) (▶ (mag_cx σ′)) (▶ (mag_cx τ′))))) (⊡ σ) (⊡ τ) (⊡ ζ))
⍝ ---- regular streams: element m within 2⁻ᵐ.  Requests below 8 are served by element 8 (the bounds ub, lb of the streams look at the
⍝ first elements, and every such look then shares one evaluation)
nats_cx ∶ 𝔖 ℕ
nats_cx ≔ (iterate (ν ↦ (⊞ ν 1)) 0)
mk_cx ∶ (ℕ → ℚ[i]) → ℝ[i]
mk_cx φ ≔ (⫶ φ nats_cx)
⍝ the same for an expensive φ: element m is φ(8⌈m/8⌉), shared by the requests m = 8k − 7 … 8k (the leaves of an expression are
⍝ requested at several nearby precisions; one evaluation serves them all)
mkq_cx ∶ (ℕ → ℚ[i]) → ℝ[i]
mkq_cx φ ≔ ((β ↦ (⫶ (μ ↦ (hd (drop (⌈ (÷ μ 111000000)) β))) nats_cx)) (⫶ (κ ↦ (φ (⊠ 111000000 κ))) nats_cx))
at_cx ∶ ℝ[i] → ℕ → ℚ[i]
at_cx ξ μ ≔ (hd (drop (max μ 111000000) ξ))
⍝ bit length of a natural number: the least j with 2ʲ > n (blen n 1 0)
blen_cx ∶ ℚ → ℚ → ℕ → ℕ
blen_cx ξ ρ ν ≔ ((≻ ρ ξ) ν (blen_cx ξ (⊠ 1100 ρ) (⊞ ν 1)))
⍝ ---- products of digit strings, the shorter factor walked digit by digit from the low end (each step adds the other factor once and
⍝ emits one digit: len₁·len₂ digit additions), and fraction arithmetic built on it (qdiv for a non-zero divisor)
mz_cx ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇
lmul_cx ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇
lmul_cx ρ ξ η ≔ (η (δ η′ ↦ ((θ ↦ (∷ (⌃ θ) (lmul_cx (⌄ θ) ξ η′))) (δ (⊞ᶻ ρ ξ) ρ))) ρ)
mz_cx ξ η ≔ ((le_cx ξ η) (lmul_cx ⊥ η ξ) (lmul_cx ⊥ ξ η))
qmul_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℚ[i] → ℚ[i]
qmul_cx ξ η ≔ (⊗ (mz_cx (◀ ξ) (◀ η)) (mz_cx (▶ ξ) (▶ η)))
qadd_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℚ[i] → ℚ[i]
qadd_cx ξ η ≔ (⊗ (⊞ᶻ (mz_cx (◀ ξ) (▶ η)) (mz_cx (◀ η) (▶ ξ))) (mz_cx (▶ ξ) (▶ η)))
qsub_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℚ[i] → ℚ[i]
qsub_cx ξ η ≔ (⊗ (⊟ᶻ (mz_cx (◀ ξ) (▶ η)) (mz_cx (◀ η) (▶ ξ))) (mz_cx (▶ ξ) (▶ η)))
qdiv_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℚ[i] → ℚ[i]
qdiv_cx ξ η ≔ (⊗ (mz_cx (◀ ξ) (▶ η)) (mz_cx (▶ ξ) (◀ η)))
⍝ ---- series.  ser t₀ β₀ ρ ρ̂ m is Σₖ tₖ (tₖ = tₖ₋₁·ρ(k)) within 2⁻ᵐ, given |t₀| ≤ β₀, |ρ(k)| ≤ ρ̂(k) ≤ 1/2 (k ≥ 1).  The partial sum
⍝ and the term share a denominator; each step multiplies by the (short) numerator and denominator of ρ(k) and truncates both at
⍝ w = m + 6 + bitlength(m + 4 + ⌈β₀⌉) (error 2⁻ʷ each).  The sum stops after term n when the bound βₙ = β₀·ρ̂(1)⋯ρ̂(n) ≤ 2⁻ᵐ⁻³ (the tail
⍝ is at most βₙ); n < 2^(w−m−6), so the error is ≤ 2n·2⁻ʷ + 2⁻ᵐ⁻³ + 2⁻ᵐ⁻¹ (final truncation) < 2⁻ᵐ.
serl_cx ∶ (ℚ[i] → ℚ[i]) → (ℚ[i] → ℚ) → ℚ → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → ℚ[i] → ℚ → ℚ[i]
serl_cx ρ ϱ ε ψ σ τ ζ ν β ≔ ((leq_cx β ε) (⊗ σ ζ) ((ν′ ↦ ((χ ↦ ((θ ι ↦ (trj_cx ψ (⊞ᶻ (⊠ᶻ σ ι) θ) θ (⊠ᶻ ζ ι) (σ′ τ′ ζ′ ↦ (serl_cx ρ ϱ ε ψ σ′ τ′ ζ′ ν′ (⊠ β (ϱ ν′)))))) (⊠ᶻ τ (◀ χ)) (▶ χ))) (ρ ν′))) (⊞ ν 1)))
ser_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℚ → (ℚ[i] → ℚ[i]) → (ℚ[i] → ℚ) → ℕ → ℚ[i]
ser_cx ξ β ρ ϱ μ ≔ ((ψ ↦ (tr_cx (trj_cx ψ (◀ ξ) (◀ ξ) (▶ ξ) (σ τ ζ ↦ (serl_cx ρ ϱ (÷ 1 (^ 1100 (⊞ μ 1101))) ψ σ τ ζ 0 β))) (⊞ μ 1))) (rul2_cx (⊞ (⊞ μ 111011100) (blen_cx (⊞ (⊞ μ 111010000) (⌈ β)) 1 0)) 111010001))
⍝ ---- comparisons of real fractions with real numerator and denominator (of any signs): two multiplications and a sign, no conjugate
neg_cx ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔹
neg_cx ξ ≔ ((⋚ʳ ξ) ⊤ ⊥ ⊥)
leq_cx ∶ ℚ → ℚ → 𝔹
leq_cx ξ η ≔ ((δ ↦ ((⊻ (neg_cx (▶ ξ)) (neg_cx (▶ η))) ((⋚ʳ δ) ⊤ ⊤ ⊥) ((⋚ʳ δ) ⊥ ⊤ ⊤))) (⊟ᶻ (mz_cx (◀ η) (▶ ξ)) (mz_cx (◀ ξ) (▶ η))))
lt_cx ∶ ℚ → ℚ → 𝔹
lt_cx ξ η ≔ (¬ (leq_cx η ξ))
isneg_cx ∶ ℚ → 𝔹
isneg_cx ξ ≔ (⊻ (neg_cx (◀ ξ)) (neg_cx (▶ ξ)))
⍝ |x| written with a numerator and a denominator ≥ 0
pos_cx ∶ ℚ → ℚ
pos_cx ξ ≔ (⊗ ((neg_cx (◀ ξ)) (⊖ᶻ (◀ ξ)) (◀ ξ)) ((neg_cx (▶ ξ)) (⊖ᶻ (▶ ξ)) (▶ ξ)))
⍝ ---- the logarithm of 2 and π (global streams: every element is computed once)
⍝ ln 2 = 2·artanh(1/3) = Σ 2/((2k+1)·3^(2k+1))
ln2_cx ∶ ℝ
ln2_cx ≔ (mkq_cx (μ ↦ (ser_cx (÷ 1100 1101) (÷ 1100 1101) (ν ↦ (÷ (⊟ (⊠ 1100 ν) 1) (⊠ 111000001 (⊞ (⊠ 1100 ν) 1)))) (ν ↦ (÷ 1 111000001)) μ)))
⍝ arctangent series Σ (−1)ᵏ u^(2k+1)/(2k+1), given |u| ≤ b and u² ≤ b² ≤ 1/2
atser_cx ∶ ℚ → ℚ → ℚ → ℕ → ℚ
atser_cx υ β ϱ μ ≔ ((ω ↦ (ser_cx υ β (ν ↦ (÷ (⊠ ω (⊟ (⊠ 1100 ν) 1)) (⊞ (⊠ 1100 ν) 1))) (ν ↦ ϱ) μ)) (⊖ (⊠ υ υ)))
⍝ Machin: π = 16·atan(1/5) − 4·atan(1/239)
pi_cx ∶ ℝ
pi_cx ≔ (mkq_cx (μ ↦ (tr_cx (qsub_cx (⊠ (atser_cx (÷ 1 111010001) (÷ 1 111010001) (÷ 1 110011000001) (⊞ μ 111011100)) 100000000) (⊠ (atser_cx (÷ 1 10001110100011101) (÷ 1 10001110100011101) (÷ 1 100011100000111010000110000000001) (⊞ μ 111010000)) 111010000)) (⊞ μ 1))))
⍝ ---- e^z for an exact z: halve j times until |z/2ʲ| ≤ 1/2, sum the series, square j times.  With R ≥ |Re z| and B = ⌈3R/2⌉ every
⍝ intermediate e^(z/2ⁱ) lies between 2⁻ᴮ and 2ᴮ in modulus; working at W = max(m, 10) + 2B + j + 4 the relative error at most doubles
⍝ per squaring, so the result is within 2⁻ᵐ⁻¹ before the final truncation.
hb_cx ∶ ℚ → ℚ → ℕ → 𝔓 ℕ ℚ
hb_cx η ρ ν ≔ ((leq_cx (⊠ 1100 η) ρ) (⊗ ν ρ) (hb_cx η (⊠ 1100 ρ) (⊞ ν 1)))
sqj_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℕ → ℕ → ℚ[i]
sqj_cx ξ ν μ ≔ ((≐ ν 0) ξ (sqj_cx (tr_cx (⊠ ξ ξ) μ) (⊟ ν 1) μ))
expqz_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℕ → ℚ[i]
expqz_cx ξ μ ≔ ((ϱ υ ↦ ((ρ₂ ↦ ((ω ↦ ((ρ₃ ↦ (tr_cx (sqj_cx (ser_cx 1 1 (ν ↦ (÷ ω ν)) (ν ↦ (÷ υ (⊠ (▶ ρ₂) ν))) ρ₃) (◀ ρ₂) ρ₃) (⊞ μ 1))) (⊞ (⊞ (max μ 111001100) (⊠ 1100 (⌈ (⊠ (÷ 1101 1100) ϱ)))) (⊞ (◀ ρ₂) 111010000)))) (÷ ξ (▶ ρ₂)))) (hb_cx υ 1 0))) (⌈ (abs (ℜ ξ))) (⌈ (⊞ (abs (ℜ ξ)) (abs (ℑ ξ)))))
⍝ an approximant argument is first truncated at m + B + 3 (B = ⌈3/2·(|Re z| + 1)⌉: |e^w| ≤ 2ᴮ near z), then e^z′ at m + 1
expq_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℕ → ℚ[i]
expq_cx ξ μ ≔ (expqz_cx (tr_cx ξ (⊞ (⊞ μ (⌈ (⊠ (÷ 1101 1100) (⊞ (abs (ℜ ξ)) 1)))) 1101)) (⊞ μ 1))
⍝ ---- log x for x > 0 (exact or an approximant; numerator and denominator real):  x = 2ᵏ·y with 2/3 ≤ y ≤ 4/3,
⍝ log y = 2·artanh u, u = (y − 1)/(y + 1), |u| ≤ 1/5;  the scaling works on the digits of p and q (y = p/q, u = (p − q)/(p + q)).
⍝ u is truncated at m + 4 (d(2 artanh u)/du ≤ 2.09, so that costs ≤ 2⁻ᵐ⁻²·⁹; then |u| ≤ 0.2625, |2u| ≤ 3/5, u² ≤ 1/14) and the series
⍝ taken at m + 4: log y within 2⁻ᵐ⁻², k·log 2 within 2⁻ᵐ⁻², the final truncation 2⁻ᵐ⁻¹
scl_cx ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → ℤ → 𝔓 ℚ ℤ
scl_cx π₁ κ₁ ν ≔ ((¬ (⩾ᶻ (⊠ᶻ κ₁ (◀ 111010000)) (⊠ᶻ π₁ (◀ 1101)))) (scl_cx π₁ (⊠ᶻ κ₁ (◀ 1100)) (⊞ ν 1)) ((¬ (⩾ᶻ (⊠ᶻ π₁ (◀ 1101)) (⊠ᶻ κ₁ (◀ 1100)))) (scl_cx (⊠ᶻ π₁ (◀ 1100)) κ₁ (⊟ ν 1)) (⊗ (⊗ (⊟ᶻ π₁ κ₁) (⊞ᶻ π₁ κ₁)) ν)))
logpos_cx ∶ ℚ → ℕ → ℚ
logpos_cx ξ μ ≔ ((κ₁ ↦ ((υ ↦ ((σ ↦ ((≐ (▶ κ₁) 0) (tr_cx σ (⊞ μ 1)) (tr_cx (qadd_cx (⊠ (ln2a_cx (⊞ (⊞ μ 1100) (blen_cx (abs (▶ κ₁)) 1 0))) (▶ κ₁)) σ) (⊞ μ 1)))) (ser_cx (⊠ υ 1100) (÷ 1101 111010001) (ν ↦ (÷ (⊠ (⊠ υ υ) (⊟ (⊠ 1100 ν) 1)) (⊞ (⊠ 1100 ν) 1))) (ν ↦ (÷ 1 111010010)) (⊞ μ 111010000)))) (tr_cx (◀ κ₁) (⊞ μ 111010000)))) ((ζ ↦ (scl_cx (◀ ζ) (▶ ζ) 0)) (pos_cx ξ)))
⍝ ---- arctangent of a real x (exact or an approximant): |x| ≤ 1/2 directly; 1/2 < |x| ≤ 1: π/4 + atan((|x| − 1)/(|x| + 1));
⍝ |x| > 1: π/2 − atan(1/|x|).  The argument is first truncated at m + 3 (atan has Lipschitz constant 1)
atp_cx ∶ ℚ → ℕ → ℚ
atp_cx ξ μ ≔ ((lt_cx (÷ 1 1100) ξ) (tr_cx (qadd_cx (÷ (pia_cx (⊞ μ 111010000)) 111010000) (atser_cx (⊗ (⊟ᶻ (◀ ξ) (▶ ξ)) (⊞ᶻ (◀ ξ) (▶ ξ))) (÷ 1 1101) (÷ 1 111000001) (⊞ μ 1100))) (⊞ μ 1)) (atser_cx ξ (÷ 1 1100) (÷ 1 111010000) μ))
atpos_cx ∶ ℚ → ℕ → ℚ
atpos_cx ξ μ ≔ ((lt_cx 1 ξ) (tr_cx (qsub_cx (÷ (pia_cx (⊞ μ 1101)) 1100) (atp_cx (⊗ (▶ ξ) (◀ ξ)) (⊞ μ 1100))) (⊞ μ 1)) (atp_cx ξ μ))
atanq_cx ∶ ℚ → ℕ → ℚ
atanq_cx ξ μ ≔ ((ξ′ ↦ ((isneg_cx ξ′) (⊖ (atpos_cx (pos_cx ξ′) (⊞ μ 1))) (atpos_cx (pos_cx ξ′) (⊞ μ 1)))) (tr_cx ξ (⊞ μ 1101)))
⍝ ---- √x for x > 0 (exact or an approximant): x = 4ᵏ·y with 1/4 ≤ y ≤ 1, Newton z ← (z + y/z)/2 from z₀ = (1 + y)/2 with the
⍝ precision doubling: to reach 2⁻ᵂ take one step, with y truncated at W + 3, from the root at ⌈(W + 3)/2⌉ (from z₀ when W ≤ 4):
⍝ error ≤ (4/3)·e² + (4/3)·2⁻ᵂ⁻³ + 2⁻ᵂ⁻¹ ≤ 2⁻ᵂ, as z ≥ 3/8 near √y ∈ [1/2, 1] and e(z₀) ≤ 1/8
sc4_cx ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → ℤ → 𝔓 ℚ ℤ
sc4_cx π₁ κ₁ ν ≔ ((¬ (⩾ᶻ κ₁ π₁)) (sc4_cx π₁ (⊠ᶻ κ₁ (◀ 111010000)) (⊞ ν 1)) ((¬ (⩾ᶻ (⊠ᶻ π₁ (◀ 111010000)) κ₁)) (sc4_cx (⊠ᶻ π₁ (◀ 111010000)) κ₁ (⊟ ν 1)) (⊗ (⊗ π₁ κ₁) ν)))
nwt_cx ∶ ℚ → ℚ → ℚ
nwt_cx ψ ζ ≔ ((π₁ κ₁ ↦ (⊗ (⊞ᶻ (mz_cx (⊠ᶻ π₁ π₁) (▶ ψ)) (mz_cx (⊠ᶻ κ₁ κ₁) (◀ ψ))) (mz_cx (mz_cx π₁ κ₁) (⊠ᶻ (▶ ψ) (◀ 1100))))) (◀ ζ) (▶ ζ))
nw_cx ∶ ℚ → ℕ → ℚ
nw_cx ψ μ ≔ ((θ ↦ (tr_cx (nwt_cx θ ((⩽ μ 111010000) (⊗ (⊞ᶻ (◀ θ) (▶ θ)) (⊠ᶻ (▶ θ) (◀ 1100))) (nw_cx θ (div (⊞ μ 111010000) 1100)))) (⊞ μ 1))) (tr_cx ψ (⊞ μ 1101)))
sqrtpos_cx ∶ ℚ → ℕ → ℚ
sqrtpos_cx ξ μ ≔ ((∅ᶻ (◀ ξ)) 0 ((κ₁ ↦ (tr_cx (⊠ (nw_cx (◀ κ₁) (⊞ (max (⊞ μ (▶ κ₁)) 0) 1)) (^ 1100 (▶ κ₁))) (⊞ μ 1))) ((ζ ↦ (sc4_cx (◀ ζ) (▶ ζ) 0)) (pos_cx ξ))))
⍝ π and ln 2 at a precision of at least m: requests are rounded up to a multiple of 16 so that they share elements
pia_cx ∶ ℕ → ℚ
pia_cx μ ≔ (tr_cx (at_cx pi_cx (⊠ 111000000 (div (⊞ μ 111000001) 111000000))) (⊞ μ 1))
ln2a_cx ∶ ℕ → ℚ
ln2a_cx μ ≔ (tr_cx (at_cx ln2_cx (⊠ 111000000 (div (⊞ μ 111000001) 111000000))) (⊞ μ 1))
⍝ ---- regular-stream arithmetic.  ub x: an e ≥ 0 with |x| ≤ 2ᵉ (e = ⌈(hp − lq)/2⌉ from the magnitudes of p and q);  ubs X: the same
⍝ for a regular stream (|X| ≤ |X₀| + 1);  lb X: the first k with |Xₖ| > 2¹⁻ᵏ, so |X| > 2⁻ᵏ (it diverges if X = 0)
ub_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℕ
ub_cx ξ ≔ (div (⊞ (ℓ (excess_cx (▶ (magp_cx (⊡ (◀ ξ)))) (◀ (magp_cx (⊡ (▶ ξ)))))) 1) 1100)
ubs_cx ∶ ℝ[i] → ℕ
ubs_cx ξ ≔ (⊞ (ub_cx (at_cx ξ 0)) 1)
lbk_cx ∶ ℝ[i] → ℕ → ℕ
lbk_cx ξ ν ≔ ((lt_cx (^ 111010000 (⊟ 1 ν)) (𝒩 (at_cx ξ ν))) ν (lbk_cx ξ (⊞ ν 1)))
lb_cx ∶ ℝ[i] → ℕ
lb_cx ξ ≔ (lbk_cx ξ 0)
⍝ the least ℓ ≥ 0 with x ≥ 4⁻ˡ for an exact x > 0
lbq_cx ∶ ℚ → ℕ → ℕ
lbq_cx ξ ν ≔ ((leq_cx (^ 111010000 (⊖ ν)) ξ) ν (lbq_cx ξ (⊞ ν 1)))
sumR_cx ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
sumR_cx ξ η ≔ (mk_cx (μ ↦ (tr_cx (qadd_cx (at_cx ξ (⊞ μ 1100)) (at_cx η (⊞ μ 1100))) (⊞ μ 1))))
difR_cx ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
difR_cx ξ η ≔ (mk_cx (μ ↦ (tr_cx (qsub_cx (at_cx ξ (⊞ μ 1100)) (at_cx η (⊞ μ 1100))) (⊞ μ 1))))
⍝ x + i·y from two real streams
cpxR_cx ∶ ℝ → ℝ → ℝ[i]
cpxR_cx ξ η ≔ (mk_cx (μ ↦ (tr_cx (qadd_cx (at_cx ξ (⊞ μ 1100)) (⊠ (at_cx η (⊞ μ 1100)) 11)) (⊞ μ 1))))
reR_cx ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ
reR_cx ξ ≔ (mk_cx (μ ↦ (tr_cx (ℜ (at_cx ξ (⊞ μ 1))) (⊞ μ 1))))
imR_cx ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ
imR_cx ξ ≔ (mk_cx (μ ↦ (tr_cx (ℑ (at_cx ξ (⊞ μ 1))) (⊞ μ 1))))
sclR_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
sclR_cx κ ξ ≔ ((ν ↦ (mk_cx (μ ↦ (tr_cx (qmul_cx (at_cx ξ (⊞ μ ν)) κ) (⊞ μ 1))))) (⊞ (ub_cx κ) 1))
mulR_cx ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
mulR_cx ξ η ≔ ((ν₁ ν₂ ↦ (mk_cx (μ ↦ (tr_cx (qmul_cx (at_cx ξ (⊞ μ (⊞ ν₂ 1100))) (at_cx η (⊞ μ (⊞ ν₁ 1101)))) (⊞ μ 1))))) (ubs_cx ξ) (ubs_cx η))
invR_cx ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
invR_cx ξ ≔ ((ν ↦ (mk_cx (μ ↦ (tr_cx ((θ ↦ (⊗ (▶ θ) (◀ θ))) (at_cx ξ (⊞ μ (⊞ (⊠ 1100 ν) 1100)))) (⊞ μ 1))))) (lb_cx ξ))
divR_cx ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
divR_cx ξ η ≔ (mulR_cx ξ (invR_cx η))
⍝ ---- the elementary functions of a regular-stream argument (each with its Lipschitz bound)
⍝ e^u: with B = ⌈3/2·(|Re u₀| + 1)⌉, |e^u| ≤ 2ᴮ and |e^ũ − e^u| ≤ 2ᴮ⁺¹|ũ − u|
expR_cx ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
expR_cx ξ ≔ ((ν ↦ (mk_cx (μ ↦ (expq_cx (at_cx ξ (⊞ μ ν)) (⊞ μ 1))))) (⊞ (⌈ (⊠ (÷ 1101 1100) (⊞ (abs (ℜ (hd ξ))) 1))) 1100))
⍝ log y for a real y > 0 (|y| > 2⁻ˡ):  |log ỹ − log y| ≤ 2ˡ⁺¹|ỹ − y|
logR_cx ∶ ℝ → ℝ
logR_cx ξ ≔ ((ν ↦ (mk_cx (μ ↦ (logpos_cx (ℜ (at_cx ξ (⊞ μ ν))) (⊞ μ 1))))) (⊞ (lb_cx ξ) 1100))
⍝ √v for a real v > 0 (v > 2⁻ˡ):  |√ṽ − √v| ≤ 2^(ℓ/2)·|ṽ − v|
sqrtR_cx ∶ ℝ → ℝ
sqrtR_cx ξ ≔ ((ν ↦ (mk_cx (μ ↦ (sqrtpos_cx (ℜ (at_cx ξ (⊞ μ ν))) (⊞ μ 1))))) (⊞ (div (⊞ (lb_cx ξ) 1) 1100) 1))
⍝ atan t for a real t: Lipschitz 1
atanR_cx ∶ ℝ → ℝ
atanR_cx ξ ≔ (mk_cx (μ ↦ (atanq_cx (ℜ (at_cx ξ (⊞ μ 1))) (⊞ μ 1))))
⍝ asinh t = sgn t·log(|t| + √(t² + 1)) for a real t (exact or an approximant): u = |t| + √(t² + 1) ≥ 1, so log has Lipschitz
⍝ constant 1 near u; with √ at m + 2 and log at m + 1 the error is ≤ 2⁻ᵐ⁻¹ + 1.07·2⁻ᵐ⁻² < 2⁻ᵐ.  Lipschitz 1 in t.
asinhq_cx ∶ ℚ → ℕ → ℚ
asinhq_cx ξ μ ≔ ((θ ↦ ((isneg_cx ξ) (⊖ θ) θ)) ((υ ↦ (logpos_cx (qadd_cx υ (sqrtpos_cx (⊞ (⊠ υ υ) 1) (⊞ μ 1100))) (⊞ μ 1))) (pos_cx ξ)))
asinhR_cx ∶ ℝ → ℝ
asinhR_cx ξ ≔ (mk_cx (μ ↦ (asinhq_cx (ℜ (at_cx ξ (⊞ μ 1))) (⊞ μ 1))))
⍝ acosh x = log(x + √(x² − 1)) for x ≥ 1, the same way
acoshq_cx ∶ ℚ → ℕ → ℚ
acoshq_cx ξ μ ≔ (logpos_cx (qadd_cx ξ (sqrtpos_cx (⊟ (⊠ ξ ξ) 1) (⊞ μ 1100))) (⊞ μ 1))
⍝ ---- exact arguments: atan2, complex logarithm, complex square root
atan2q_cx ∶ ℚ → ℚ → ℕ → ℚ
atan2q_cx η ξ μ ≔ ((⋚ ξ 0) ((⩾ η 0) (tr_cx (qadd_cx (atanq_cx (÷ η ξ) (⊞ μ 1100)) (pia_cx (⊞ μ 1100))) (⊞ μ 1)) (tr_cx (qsub_cx (atanq_cx (÷ η ξ) (⊞ μ 1100)) (pia_cx (⊞ μ 1100))) (⊞ μ 1))) ((⋚ η 0) (⊖ (÷ (pia_cx (⊞ μ 1)) 1100)) 0 (÷ (pia_cx (⊞ μ 1)) 1100)) (atanq_cx (÷ η ξ) μ))
logq_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℕ → ℚ[i]
logq_cx ξ μ ≔ ((≐ ξ 0) 0 (tr_cx (qadd_cx (÷ (logpos_cx (𝒩 ξ) (⊞ μ 1100)) 1100) (⊠ (atan2q_cx (ℑ ξ) (ℜ ξ) (⊞ μ 1100)) 11)) (⊞ μ 1)))
⍝ principal √z: for z = a + bi (b ≠ 0) with u = √((|z| + |a|)/2) and v = |b|/(2u):  √z = u + i·sgn(b)·v (a ≥ 0),  v + i·sgn(b)·u (a < 0);
⍝ √(max(|a|, |b|)/2) ≥ 2⁻ˡ bounds u from below, so |z| is taken at m + ℓ + 4.  On the cut (b = 0, a < 0) the value is i√|a|.
sqrtq_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℕ → ℚ[i]
sqrtq_cx ξ μ ≔ ((ϕ ψ ↦ ((≐ ψ 0) ((⩾ ϕ 0) (sqrtpos_cx ϕ μ) (⊠ 11 (sqrtpos_cx (⊖ ϕ) μ))) ((ν ↦ ((υ ↦ ((υ′ ↦ ((⩾ ϕ 0) (tr_cx (qadd_cx υ (⊠ υ′ ((⩾ ψ 0) 11 111))) (⊞ μ 1)) (tr_cx (qadd_cx υ′ (⊠ υ ((⩾ ψ 0) 11 111))) (⊞ μ 1)))) (qdiv_cx (abs ψ) (⊠ υ 1100)))) (sqrtpos_cx (÷ (qadd_cx (sqrtpos_cx (𝒩 ξ) (⊞ μ (⊞ ν 111010000))) (abs ϕ)) 1100) (⊞ μ 111010001)))) (lbq_cx (÷ (max (abs ϕ) (abs ψ)) 1100) 0)))) (ℜ ξ) (ℑ ξ))
⍝ ---- more regular-stream tools: conjugate and negative (pointwise, the error is unchanged), |X|², atan2 and log of streams
conjR_cx ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
conjR_cx ≔ (⫶ ∗)
negR_cx ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
negR_cx ≔ (⫶ ⊖)
⍝ |X|² (|X| ≤ 2^ν):  ||X̃|² − |X|²| ≤ δ(2|X| + δ), so X is taken at m + ν + 3
normR_cx ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ
normR_cx ξ ≔ ((ν ↦ (mk_cx (μ ↦ (tr_cx (𝒩 (at_cx ξ (⊞ μ ν))) (⊞ μ 1))))) (⊞ (ubs_cx ξ) 1101))
⍝ atan2(Y, X) of real streams with (X, Y) ≠ (0, 0) (|(X, Y)| > 2⁻ᵏ): the point is taken at m + k + 3, so it stays 2⁻ᵏ⁻¹ away from the
⍝ origin and the angle moves by at most √2·2⁻ᵐ⁻² (the callers keep the point off the negative real axis, or Y exactly 0)
atan2R_cx ∶ ℝ → ℝ → ℝ
atan2R_cx η ξ ≔ ((κ ↦ (mk_cx (μ ↦ ((ν ↦ (atan2q_cx (ℜ (at_cx η ν)) (ℜ (at_cx ξ ν)) (⊞ μ 1))) (⊞ μ (⊞ κ 1101)))))) (lb_cx (cpxR_cx ξ η)))
⍝ principal log of a stream X ≠ 0 that stays off the negative real axis: ½·log|X|² + i·atan2(Im X, Re X)
logcR_cx ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
logcR_cx ξ ≔ (cpxR_cx (sclR_cx (÷ 1 1100) (logR_cx (normR_cx ξ))) (atan2R_cx (imR_cx ξ) (reR_cx ξ)))
⍝ sin and cos of a stream: (e^(iU) − e^(−iU))/(2i), (e^(iU) + e^(−iU))/2
sinR_cx ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
sinR_cx ξ ≔ (sclR_cx (÷ 111 1100) (difR_cx (expR_cx (sclR_cx 11 ξ)) (expR_cx (sclR_cx 111 ξ))))
cosR_cx ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
cosR_cx ξ ≔ (sclR_cx (÷ 1 1100) (sumR_cx (expR_cx (sclR_cx 11 ξ)) (expR_cx (sclR_cx 111 ξ))))
⍝ ---- regular streams of exact arguments
expS_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
expS_cx ξ ≔ (mkq_cx (μ ↦ (expq_cx ξ μ)))
logS_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
logS_cx ξ ≔ (mkq_cx (μ ↦ (logq_cx ξ μ)))
sqrtS_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
sqrtS_cx ξ ≔ (mkq_cx (μ ↦ (sqrtq_cx ξ μ)))
⍝ log x for x > 0, √x for x ≥ 0, atan2(y, x), atan x (all real and exact)
lpS_cx ∶ ℚ → ℝ
lpS_cx ξ ≔ (mkq_cx (μ ↦ (logpos_cx ξ μ)))
spS_cx ∶ ℚ → ℝ
spS_cx ξ ≔ (mkq_cx (μ ↦ (sqrtpos_cx ξ μ)))
at2S_cx ∶ ℚ → ℚ → ℝ
at2S_cx η ξ ≔ (mkq_cx (μ ↦ (atan2q_cx η ξ μ)))
atS_cx ∶ ℚ → ℝ
atS_cx ξ ≔ (mkq_cx (μ ↦ (atanq_cx ξ μ)))
⍝ ---- tests on exact values
isreal_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → 𝔹
isreal_cx ξ ≔ (≐ (ℑ ξ) 0)
isint_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → 𝔹
isint_cx ξ ≔ (∧ (isreal_cx ξ) (≐ (ℜ ξ) (⌊ (ℜ ξ))))
⍝ z is 0, −1, −2, … (a pole of Γ)
npi_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → 𝔹
npi_cx ξ ≔ (∧ (isint_cx ξ) (⩽ (ℜ ξ) 0))
⍝ an integer e with |x| ≤ 2ᵉ (it may be negative; any e will do for x = 0)
ube_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℤ
ube_cx ξ ≔ (div (⊞ (⊟ (ℓ (▶ (magp_cx (⊡ (◀ ξ))))) (ℓ (◀ (magp_cx (⊡ (▶ ξ)))))) 1) 1100)
⍝ the least integer j with x ≤ 2ʲ, for an exact x > 0
lg2u_cx ∶ ℚ → ℚ → ℤ → ℤ
lg2u_cx ξ ρ ν ≔ ((leq_cx ξ ρ) ν (lg2u_cx ξ (⊠ 1100 ρ) (⊞ ν 1)))
lg2d_cx ∶ ℚ → ℚ → ℤ → ℤ
lg2d_cx ξ ρ ν ≔ ((leq_cx ξ (÷ ρ 1100)) (lg2d_cx ξ (÷ ρ 1100) (⊟ ν 1)) ν)
lg2_cx ∶ ℚ → ℤ
lg2_cx ξ ≔ ((leq_cx ξ 1) (lg2d_cx ξ 1 0) (lg2u_cx ξ 1100 1))
⍝ an integer e with |z| ≤ 2ᵉ for an exact z ≠ 0:  ⌈½·log₂ |z|²⌉
lgz_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℤ
lgz_cx ξ ≔ (div (⊞ (lg2_cx (𝒩 ξ)) 1) 1100)
⍝ ---- series whose first terms may grow.  serE t₀ e₀ ρ r α m is Σₖ tₖ (tₖ = tₖ₋₁·ρ(k)) within 2⁻ᵐ, given |t₀| ≤ 2^e₀ and
⍝ |ρ(k)| ≤ 2^r(k) with integers r(k), non-increasing from the first k with r(k) ≤ −1 on.  It stops after term n once the bound
⍝ eₙ = e₀ + r(1) + … + r(n) ≤ −m − 3 and r(n + 1) ≤ −1 (the tail is then below 2^eₙ).  Partial sum and term share a denominator and
⍝ are truncated at w = m + 6 + α bits after each step; a truncation error is carried along by the later ratios, so the total error is
⍝ at most 2n²A·2⁻ʷ (A the largest product of consecutive |ρ(k)|): α must cover 2·log₂ n + log₂ A.
serEl_cx ∶ (ℚ[i] → ℚ[i]) → (ℚ[i] → ℤ) → ℤ → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → ℚ[i] → ℤ → ℚ[i]
serEl_cx ρ ϱ ε ψ σ τ ζ ν β ≔ ((ν′ ↦ ((θ′ ↦ ((∧ (⩽ β ε) (⩽ θ′ 11101)) (⊗ σ ζ) ((χ ↦ ((θ ι ↦ (trj_cx ψ (⊞ᶻ (⊠ᶻ σ ι) θ) θ (⊠ᶻ ζ ι) (σ′ τ′ ζ′ ↦ (serEl_cx ρ ϱ ε ψ σ′ τ′ ζ′ ν′ (⊞ β θ′))))) (⊠ᶻ τ (◀ χ)) (▶ χ))) (ρ ν′)))) (ϱ ν′))) (⊞ ν 1))
serE_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℤ → (ℚ[i] → ℚ[i]) → (ℚ[i] → ℤ) → ℕ → ℕ → ℚ[i]
serE_cx ξ ε₀ ρ ϱ α μ ≔ ((ψ ↦ (tr_cx (trj_cx ψ (◀ ξ) (◀ ξ) (▶ ξ) (σ τ ζ ↦ (serEl_cx ρ ϱ (⊖ (⊞ μ 1101)) ψ σ τ ζ 0 ε₀))) (⊞ μ 1))) (rul2_cx (⊞ (⊞ μ 111011100) α) 111010001))
⍝ the same with a fixed number n of terms t₀ … tₙ₋₁ (the caller bounds the tail; with |ρ(k)| ≤ 1 the error is at most n²·2⁻ʷ)
serNl_cx ∶ (ℚ[i] → ℚ[i]) → ℕ → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → ℚ[i] → ℚ[i]
serNl_cx ρ ε ψ σ τ ζ ν ≔ ((ν′ ↦ ((⩾ ν′ ε) (⊗ σ ζ) ((χ ↦ ((θ ι ↦ (trj_cx ψ (⊞ᶻ (⊠ᶻ σ ι) θ) θ (⊠ᶻ ζ ι) (σ′ τ′ ζ′ ↦ (serNl_cx ρ ε ψ σ′ τ′ ζ′ ν′)))) (⊠ᶻ τ (◀ χ)) (▶ χ))) (ρ ν′)))) (⊞ ν 1))
serN_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → (ℚ[i] → ℚ[i]) → ℕ → ℕ → ℕ → ℚ[i]
serN_cx ξ ρ ν α μ ≔ ((ψ ↦ (tr_cx (trj_cx ψ (◀ ξ) (◀ ξ) (▶ ξ) (σ τ ζ ↦ (serNl_cx ρ ν ψ σ τ ζ 0))) (⊞ μ 1))) (rul2_cx (⊞ (⊞ μ 111011100) α) 111010001))
⍝ ---- the constants
𝜋 ∶ ℝ   ⍝ π = 3.14159…, by Machin's formula 16·atan(1/5) − 4·atan(1/239); element n is within 2⁻ⁿ
𝜋 ≔ pi_cx
ℯ ∶ ℝ   ⍝ Euler's number e = 2.71828…; element n is within 2⁻ⁿ
ℯ ≔ (mkq_cx (μ ↦ (expq_cx 1 μ)))
⍝ ---- logarithms, powers and roots
logc ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ principal logarithm log z = log|z| + i·arg z, Im in (−π, π] (log(−x) = log x + iπ); log 0 = 0; element n within 2⁻ⁿ
logc ≔ logS_cx
logcᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ principal logarithm of a lazy argument (through the diagonal ⟐; converges off the negative real axis)
logcᴿ ≔ (⟐ logc)
logb ∶ ℚ[i] → ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ logarithm to base b: logb(b, z) = log z / log b (principal logs); 0 when b is 0 or 1
logb ξ η ≔ ((∨ (≐ ξ 0) (≐ ξ 1)) (⁂ 0) (divR_cx (logS_cx η) (logS_cx ξ)))
log₁p ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ log(1 + z) (principal); 0 at z = −1
log₁p ξ ≔ (logS_cx (⊞ 1 ξ))
log₁pᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ log(1 + z) of a lazy argument
log₁pᴿ ≔ (⟐ log₁p)
expm₁ ∶ ℚ → ℝ   ⍝ eᶻ − 1 (absolute error: element n is within 2⁻ⁿ)
expm₁ ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
expm₁ ξ ≔ (mk_cx (μ ↦ (tr_cx (⊟ (expq_cx ξ (⊞ μ 1)) 1) (⊞ μ 1))))
expm₁ᴿ ∶ ℝ → ℝ   ⍝ eᶻ − 1 of a lazy argument
expm₁ᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
expm₁ᴿ ≔ (⟐ expm₁)
⍝ wᵏ as a stream (k an integer, exact) or e^(w·log z);  0^w = 0 for w ≠ 0 and 0⁰ = 1
pow ∶ ℚ[i] → ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ principal power z^w = e^(w·log z); exact (a constant stream) for an integer w; 0^w = 0 for w ≠ 0, 0⁰ = 1
pow ξ η ≔ ((isint_cx η) (⁂ (^ ξ (ℜ η))) ((≐ ξ 0) (⁂ 0) (expR_cx (sclR_cx η (logS_cx ξ)))))
⍝ the diagonal of a function of two arguments: element n is element n of f(xₙ, yₙ)
diag2_cx ∶ (α → β → 𝔖 γ) → 𝔖 α → 𝔖 β → 𝔖 γ
diag2_cx φ ξ η ≔ (⟐ (θ ↦ (φ (◀ θ) (▶ θ))) (⫴ ⊗ ξ η))
powᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ principal power of lazy arguments (element n of pow(xₙ, yₙ))
powᴿ ≔ (diag2_cx pow)
⍝ the n-th root z^(1/n) = e^(log z / n) (principal); 0 for z = 0 or n = 0
rootS_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℚ → ℝ[i]
rootS_cx ξ ν ≔ ((∨ (≐ ξ 0) (≐ ν 0)) (⁂ 0) (expR_cx (sclR_cx (÷ 1 ν) (logS_cx ξ))))
nthroot ∶ ℚ[i] → ℤ → ℝ[i]   ⍝ principal n-th root z^(1/n) = e^(log z / n) (n may be negative); 0 for z = 0 or n = 0
nthroot ξ ν ≔ (rootS_cx ξ ν)
cbrt ∶ ℚ → ℝ   ⍝ cube root: the real root of a real x (cbrt(−8) = −2), the principal root e^(log z / 3) of a non-real z
cbrt ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
cbrt ξ ≔ ((isreal_cx ξ) ((ϕ ↦ ((⋚ ϕ 0) (negR_cx (rootS_cx (⊖ ϕ) 1101)) (⁂ 0) (rootS_cx ϕ 1101))) (ℜ ξ)) (rootS_cx ξ 1101))
cbrtᴿ ∶ ℝ → ℝ   ⍝ cube root of a lazy argument
cbrtᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
cbrtᴿ ≔ (⟐ cbrt)
⍝ e^(2πik/n): exact for k/n = 0, 1/4, 1/2, 3/4
rootu_cx ∶ ℕ → ℕ → ℝ[i]
rootu_cx ν κ ≔ ((θ ↦ ((≐ θ 0) (⁂ 1) ((≐ θ (÷ 1 111010000)) (⁂ 11) ((≐ θ (÷ 1 1100)) (⁂ 11101) ((≐ θ (÷ 1101 111010000)) (⁂ 111) (expR_cx (sclR_cx (⊠ 1110100 θ) pi_cx))))))) (÷ κ ν))
rootsofunity ∶ ℤ → 𝔏 ℝ[i]   ⍝ the n-th roots of unity e^(2πik/n), k = 0 … n − 1 (empty for n ≤ 0)
rootsofunity ν ≔ (⫶ (κ ↦ (rootu_cx ν κ)) (⍳ ν))
⍝ ---- polar form
arg ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ   ⍝ principal argument of z, in (−π, π]; arg 0 = 0
arg ξ ≔ (at2S_cx (ℑ ξ) (ℜ ξ))
argᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ   ⍝ principal argument of a lazy argument
argᴿ ≔ (⟐ arg)
atan2 ∶ ℚ → ℚ → ℝ   ⍝ atan2(y, x): the angle of the point (x, y), in (−π, π]; atan2(0, 0) = 0
atan2 ≔ at2S_cx
cis ∶ ℚ → ℝ[i]   ⍝ cis t = cos t + i·sin t = e^(it)
cis ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
cis ξ ≔ (expS_cx (⊠ 11 ξ))
cisᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ e^(it) of a lazy argument
cisᴿ ≔ (⟐ cis)
polar ∶ ℚ → ℚ → ℝ[i]   ⍝ polar(r, t) = r·e^(it)
polar ∶ ℚ[i] → ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
polar ξ η ≔ (sclR_cx ξ (expS_cx (⊠ 11 η)))
csgn ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ complex sign z/|z|; 0 at 0
csgn ξ ≔ ((≐ ξ 0) (⁂ 0) (sclR_cx ξ (spS_cx (÷ 1 (𝒩 ξ)))))
csgnᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ z/|z| of a lazy argument
csgnᴿ ≔ (⟐ csgn)
hypot ∶ ℚ → ℚ → ℝ   ⍝ hypot(x, y) = √(x² + y²) (for complex arguments √(|x|² + |y|²))
hypot ∶ ℚ[i] → ℚ[i] → ℝ
hypot ξ η ≔ (spS_cx (⊞ (𝒩 ξ) (𝒩 η)))
⍝ ---- circular functions.  For an exact z, E = e^(2iz):  tan z = −i·(1 − 2/(E + 1)),  cot z = i·(1 + 2/(E − 1));  sin z ≠ 0 and
⍝ cos z ≠ 0 for every rational z ≠ 0 (π is irrational), so the only pole is z = 0 (cot, csc), where the value is 0
sinS_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
sinS_cx ξ ≔ ((isreal_cx ξ) (imR_cx (expS_cx (⊠ 11 ξ))) (sclR_cx (÷ 111 1100) (difR_cx (expS_cx (⊠ 11 ξ)) (expS_cx (⊠ 111 ξ)))))
cosS_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
cosS_cx ξ ≔ ((isreal_cx ξ) (reR_cx (expS_cx (⊠ 11 ξ))) (sclR_cx (÷ 1 1100) (sumR_cx (expS_cx (⊠ 11 ξ)) (expS_cx (⊠ 111 ξ)))))
⍝ real part only, for a real argument (the approximants of a real value are made real)
rel_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
rel_cx ξ η ≔ ((isreal_cx ξ) (⫶ ℜ η) η)
cot ∶ ℚ → ℝ   ⍝ cotangent cos z / sin z = i·(e^(2iz) + 1)/(e^(2iz) − 1); cot 0 = 0 (pole)
cot ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
cot ξ ≔ ((≐ ξ 0) (⁂ 0) (rel_cx ξ (sclR_cx 11 (sumR_cx (⁂ 1) (sclR_cx 1100 (invR_cx (difR_cx (expS_cx (⊠ 1110100 ξ)) (⁂ 1))))))))
cotᴿ ∶ ℝ → ℝ   ⍝ cotangent of a lazy argument
cotᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
cotᴿ ≔ (⟐ cot)
sec ∶ ℚ → ℝ   ⍝ secant 1/cos z
sec ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
sec ξ ≔ (rel_cx ξ (invR_cx (cosS_cx ξ)))
secᴿ ∶ ℝ → ℝ   ⍝ secant of a lazy argument
secᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
secᴿ ≔ (⟐ sec)
csc ∶ ℚ → ℝ   ⍝ cosecant 1/sin z; csc 0 = 0 (pole)
csc ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
csc ξ ≔ ((≐ ξ 0) (⁂ 0) (rel_cx ξ (invR_cx (sinS_cx ξ))))
cscᴿ ∶ ℝ → ℝ   ⍝ cosecant of a lazy argument
cscᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
cscᴿ ≔ (⟐ csc)
tanᴿ ∶ ℝ → ℝ   ⍝ tangent of a lazy argument (the series quotient of lib/real.imo through the diagonal)
tanᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
tanᴿ ≔ (⟐ tan)
⍝ ---- hyperbolic functions.  E = e^(2z): coth z = 1 + 2/(E − 1); sinh z = 0 and cosh z = 0 have no rational root but 0 (sinh)
sinhS_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
sinhS_cx ξ ≔ (sclR_cx (÷ 1 1100) (difR_cx (expS_cx ξ) (expS_cx (⊖ ξ))))
coshS_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
coshS_cx ξ ≔ (sclR_cx (÷ 1 1100) (sumR_cx (expS_cx ξ) (expS_cx (⊖ ξ))))
coth ∶ ℚ → ℝ   ⍝ hyperbolic cotangent cosh z / sinh z = 1 + 2/(e^(2z) − 1); coth 0 = 0 (pole)
coth ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
coth ξ ≔ ((≐ ξ 0) (⁂ 0) (rel_cx ξ (sumR_cx (⁂ 1) (sclR_cx 1100 (invR_cx (difR_cx (expS_cx (⊠ 1100 ξ)) (⁂ 1)))))))
cothᴿ ∶ ℝ → ℝ   ⍝ hyperbolic cotangent of a lazy argument
cothᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
cothᴿ ≔ (⟐ coth)
sech ∶ ℚ → ℝ   ⍝ hyperbolic secant 1/cosh z
sech ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
sech ξ ≔ (rel_cx ξ (invR_cx (coshS_cx ξ)))
sechᴿ ∶ ℝ → ℝ   ⍝ hyperbolic secant of a lazy argument
sechᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
sechᴿ ≔ (⟐ sech)
csch ∶ ℚ → ℝ   ⍝ hyperbolic cosecant 1/sinh z; csch 0 = 0 (pole)
csch ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
csch ξ ≔ ((≐ ξ 0) (⁂ 0) (rel_cx ξ (invR_cx (sinhS_cx ξ))))
cschᴿ ∶ ℝ → ℝ   ⍝ hyperbolic cosecant of a lazy argument
cschᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
cschᴿ ≔ (⟐ csch)
sinhᴿ ∶ ℝ → ℝ   ⍝ hyperbolic sine of a lazy argument (the series of lib/real.imo through the diagonal)
sinhᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
sinhᴿ ≔ (⟐ sinh)
coshᴿ ∶ ℝ → ℝ   ⍝ hyperbolic cosine of a lazy argument
coshᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
coshᴿ ≔ (⟐ cosh)
tanhᴿ ∶ ℝ → ℝ   ⍝ hyperbolic tangent of a lazy argument
tanhᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
tanhᴿ ≔ (⟐ tanh)
⍝ ---- sinc z = sin z / z (sinc 0 = 1): the series Σ (−z²)ᵏ/(2k + 1)! for |z| ≤ 1, sin z · (1/z) beyond
sinc ∶ ℚ → ℝ   ⍝ sinc z = sin z / z, sinc 0 = 1 (unnormalised)
sinc ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
sinc ξ ≔ ((leq_cx (𝒩 ξ) 1) (mk_cx (μ ↦ (ser_cx 1 1 (ν ↦ (÷ (⊖ (⊠ ξ ξ)) (⊠ (⊠ 1100 ν) (⊞ (⊠ 1100 ν) 1)))) (ν ↦ (÷ 1 (⊠ (⊠ 1100 ν) (⊞ (⊠ 1100 ν) 1)))) μ))) (sclR_cx (÷ 1 ξ) (sinS_cx ξ)))
sincᴿ ∶ ℝ → ℝ   ⍝ sinc of a lazy argument
sincᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
sincᴿ ≔ (⟐ sinc)
⍝ ---- inverse circular and hyperbolic functions, principal values and branch cuts as in C99 / Python's cmath; a point on a cut
⍝ takes the value of the side of +0 (the limit from above for a cut on the real axis, from the right for one on the imaginary axis).
⍝ For exact z = x + iy the formulas below use only exact arguments for log, √ and atan2 (or square roots of exact values):
⍝   atan z  = ½·atan2(2x, 1 − x² − y²) + i·¼·log(|z + i|²/|z − i|²)      (poles ±i: value 0)
⍝   atanh z = ¼·log(|1 + z|²/|1 − z|²) + i·½·atan2(2y, 1 − x² − y²)      (poles ±1: value 0)
⍝   asinh z = asinh(Im(conj(s₁)·s₂)) + i·atan2(y, Re(s₁s₂)),  s₁ = √(1 − iz), s₂ = √(1 + iz)     (Kahan)
⍝   acos z  = 2·atan2(Re s₁, Re s₂) + i·asinh(Im(conj(s₂)·s₁)),  s₁ = √(1 − z), s₂ = √(1 + z)
⍝   acosh z = asinh(Re(conj(s₁)·s₂)) + 2i·atan2(Im s₁, Re s₂),  s₁ = √(z − 1), s₂ = √(z + 1)
⍝   asin z  = −i·asinh(iz)
⍝ with the values on the cuts written out:  asin x = sgn(x)·π/2 + i·acosh|x|,  acos x = −i·acosh x (x > 1), π − i·acosh|x| (x < −1),
⍝ asinh(iy) = acosh|y| + i·sgn(y)·π/2  (|x|, |y| > 1).
⍝ asinh t of a real stream (exists: asinhR_cx); asinh and acosh of an exact real
asinhX_cx ∶ ℚ → ℝ
asinhX_cx ξ ≔ (mkq_cx (μ ↦ (asinhq_cx ξ μ)))
acoshX_cx ∶ ℚ → ℝ
acoshX_cx ξ ≔ (mkq_cx (μ ↦ (acoshq_cx ξ μ)))
⍝ π/2 as a stream
pih_cx ∶ ℝ
pih_cx ≔ (sclR_cx (÷ 1 1100) pi_cx)
⍝ |s₁| + |s₂| ≤ 2^U for the square roots s₁,₂ of 1 ∓ w, z ∓ 1 (|w| = |z|): |sᵢ|⁴ ≤ (1 + |z|)² ≤ 2 + 2|z|²
ukh_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℤ
ukh_cx ξ ≔ (⊞ (div (⊞ (lg2_cx (⊞ 1100 (⊠ 1100 (𝒩 ξ)))) 1101) 111010000) 1)
⍝ the formulas above at one precision: s₁, s₂ are taken within 2⁻ᵖ, p = m + 5 + U (+ L): a product such as conj(s₁)·s₂ then moves by
⍝ at most 2^(U+1−p) ≤ 2⁻ᵐ⁻⁴, asinh has Lipschitz constant 1, atan2 at most 1 where its point stays ≥ 1 from the origin (acos: Re s₁,
⍝ Re s₂; acosh: Re s₂, Im s₁ — the squares sum to (|z − 1| + |z + 1| + 2)/2 ≥ 2) and 1/|y| for asinh's atan2(y, Re(s₁s₂))
⍝ (2^L ≥ 1/|y|); every part is then within 2⁻ᵐ⁻², and the final truncation adds 2⁻ᵐ⁻¹.  S₁, S₂ are the streams of s₁, s₂.
asinhF_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i] → ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
asinhF_cx ξ σ₁ σ₂ ≔ ((ψ ↦ ((ν ↦ (mk_cx (μ ↦ ((τ₁ τ₂ ↦ (tr_cx (⊞ (asinhq_cx (ℑ (⊠ (∗ τ₁) τ₂)) (⊞ μ 1100)) (⊠ 11 (atan2q_cx ψ (ℜ (⊠ τ₁ τ₂)) (⊞ μ 1101)))) (⊞ μ 1))) (at_cx σ₁ (⊞ μ ν)) (at_cx σ₂ (⊞ μ ν)))))) (⊞ (⊞ 111010001 (ukh_cx ξ)) (max 0 (⊟ 1 (lgz_cx ψ)))))) (ℑ ξ))
acosF_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i] → ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
acosF_cx ξ σ₁ σ₂ ≔ ((ν ↦ (mk_cx (μ ↦ ((τ₁ τ₂ ↦ (tr_cx (⊞ (⊠ 1100 (atan2q_cx (ℜ τ₁) (ℜ τ₂) (⊞ μ 1101))) (⊠ 11 (asinhq_cx (ℑ (⊠ (∗ τ₂) τ₁)) (⊞ μ 1100)))) (⊞ μ 1))) (at_cx σ₁ (⊞ μ ν)) (at_cx σ₂ (⊞ μ ν)))))) (⊞ 111010001 (ukh_cx ξ)))
acoshF_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i] → ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
acoshF_cx ξ σ₁ σ₂ ≔ ((ν ↦ (mk_cx (μ ↦ ((τ₁ τ₂ ↦ (tr_cx (⊞ (asinhq_cx (ℜ (⊠ (∗ τ₁) τ₂)) (⊞ μ 1100)) (⊠ 1110100 (atan2q_cx (ℑ τ₁) (ℜ τ₂) (⊞ μ 1101)))) (⊞ μ 1))) (at_cx σ₁ (⊞ μ ν)) (at_cx σ₂ (⊞ μ ν)))))) (⊞ 111010001 (ukh_cx ξ)))
asinhC_cx ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
asinhC_cx ξ ≔ ((ϕ ψ ↦ ((∧ (≐ ϕ 0) (lt_cx 1 (abs ψ))) (cpxR_cx (acoshX_cx (abs ψ)) ((⩾ ψ 0) pih_cx (negR_cx pih_cx))) (asinhF_cx ξ (sqrtS_cx (⊟ 1 (⊠ 11 ξ))) (sqrtS_cx (⊞ 1 (⊠ 11 ξ)))))) (ℜ ξ) (ℑ ξ))
asinh ∶ ℚ → ℝ   ⍝ inverse hyperbolic sine (principal; cuts on the imaginary axis beyond ±i, as in cmath)
asinh ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
asinh ξ ≔ ((isreal_cx ξ) (asinhX_cx (ℜ ξ)) (asinhC_cx ξ))
asinhᴿ ∶ ℝ → ℝ   ⍝ inverse hyperbolic sine of a lazy argument
asinhᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
asinhᴿ ≔ (⟐ asinh)
asin ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ inverse sine (principal; cuts (−∞, −1) and (1, ∞) as in cmath: asin x = sgn x·π/2 + i·acosh|x| there)
asin ξ ≔ ((ϕ ψ ↦ ((≐ ψ 0) ((leq_cx (abs ϕ) 1) (atan2R_cx (⁂ ϕ) (spS_cx (⊟ 1 (⊠ ϕ ϕ)))) (cpxR_cx ((⩾ ϕ 0) pih_cx (negR_cx pih_cx)) (acoshX_cx (abs ϕ)))) (sclR_cx 111 (asinh (⊠ 11 ξ))))) (ℜ ξ) (ℑ ξ))
asinᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ inverse sine of a lazy argument
asinᴿ ≔ (⟐ asin)
acos ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ inverse cosine (principal; cuts as asin: acos x = −i·acosh x for x > 1, π − i·acosh|x| for x < −1)
acos ξ ≔ ((ϕ ψ ↦ ((≐ ψ 0) ((leq_cx (abs ϕ) 1) (atan2R_cx (spS_cx (⊟ 1 (⊠ ϕ ϕ))) (⁂ ϕ)) ((⩾ ϕ 0) (cpxR_cx (⁂ 0) (negR_cx (acoshX_cx ϕ))) (cpxR_cx pi_cx (negR_cx (acoshX_cx (⊖ ϕ)))))) (acosF_cx ξ (sqrtS_cx (⊟ 1 ξ)) (sqrtS_cx (⊞ 1 ξ))))) (ℜ ξ) (ℑ ξ))
acosᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ inverse cosine of a lazy argument
acosᴿ ≔ (⟐ acos)
atanc ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ inverse tangent of a complex z (principal; cuts on the imaginary axis beyond ±i, as in cmath); 0 at the poles ±i
atanc ξ ≔ ((ϕ ψ ↦ ((∧ (≐ ϕ 0) (≐ (abs ψ) 1)) (⁂ 0) ((θ ↦ ((≐ ψ 0) θ (cpxR_cx θ (sclR_cx (÷ 1 111010000) (lpS_cx (÷ (𝒩 (⊞ ξ 11)) (𝒩 (⊟ ξ 11)))))))) (sclR_cx (÷ 1 1100) (at2S_cx (⊠ 1100 ϕ) (⊟ (⊟ 1 (⊠ ϕ ϕ)) (⊠ ψ ψ))))))) (ℜ ξ) (ℑ ξ))
atancᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ inverse tangent of a lazy complex argument
atancᴿ ≔ (⟐ atanc)
acot ∶ ℚ → ℝ   ⍝ inverse cotangent atan(1/z) (principal; acot 0 = π/2; 0 at the poles ±i)
acot ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
acot ξ ≔ ((ϕ ψ ↦ ((∧ (≐ ϕ 0) (≐ (abs ψ) 1)) (⁂ 0) ((θ ↦ ((≐ ψ 0) θ (cpxR_cx θ (sclR_cx (÷ 1 111010000) (lpS_cx (÷ (𝒩 (⊞ 1 (⊠ 11 ξ))) (𝒩 (⊟ 1 (⊠ 11 ξ))))))))) (sclR_cx (÷ 1 1100) (at2S_cx (⊠ 1100 ϕ) (⊟ (𝒩 ξ) 1)))))) (ℜ ξ) (ℑ ξ))
acotᴿ ∶ ℝ → ℝ   ⍝ inverse cotangent of a lazy argument
acotᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
acotᴿ ≔ (⟐ acot)
asec ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ inverse secant acos(1/z); 0 at z = 0 (pole)
asec ξ ≔ ((≐ ξ 0) (⁂ 0) (acos (÷ 1 ξ)))
asecᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ inverse secant of a lazy argument
asecᴿ ≔ (⟐ asec)
acsc ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ inverse cosecant asin(1/z); 0 at z = 0 (pole)
acsc ξ ≔ ((≐ ξ 0) (⁂ 0) (asin (÷ 1 ξ)))
acscᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ inverse cosecant of a lazy argument
acscᴿ ≔ (⟐ acsc)
acosh ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ inverse hyperbolic cosine (principal; cut (−∞, 1) as in cmath: acosh x = i·acos x on [−1, 1), acosh|x| + iπ below −1)
acosh ξ ≔ ((ϕ ψ ↦ ((≐ ψ 0) ((⩾ ϕ 1) (acoshX_cx ϕ) ((⩾ ϕ 11101) (cpxR_cx (⁂ 0) (atan2R_cx (spS_cx (⊟ 1 (⊠ ϕ ϕ))) (⁂ ϕ))) (cpxR_cx (acoshX_cx (⊖ ϕ)) pi_cx))) (acoshF_cx ξ (sqrtS_cx (⊟ ξ 1)) (sqrtS_cx (⊞ ξ 1))))) (ℜ ξ) (ℑ ξ))
acoshᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ inverse hyperbolic cosine of a lazy argument
acoshᴿ ≔ (⟐ acosh)
atanh ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ inverse hyperbolic tangent (principal; cuts (−∞, −1) and (1, ∞), value with Im = +π/2 there, as in cmath); 0 at ±1
atanh ξ ≔ ((ϕ ψ ↦ ((∧ (≐ ψ 0) (≐ (abs ϕ) 1)) (⁂ 0) ((θ ↦ ((∧ (≐ ψ 0) (lt_cx (abs ϕ) 1)) θ (cpxR_cx θ (sclR_cx (÷ 1 1100) (at2S_cx (⊠ 1100 ψ) (⊟ (⊟ 1 (⊠ ϕ ϕ)) (⊠ ψ ψ))))))) (sclR_cx (÷ 1 111010000) (lpS_cx (÷ (𝒩 (⊞ 1 ξ)) (𝒩 (⊟ 1 ξ)))))))) (ℜ ξ) (ℑ ξ))
atanhᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ inverse hyperbolic tangent of a lazy argument
atanhᴿ ≔ (⟐ atanh)
acoth ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ inverse hyperbolic cotangent atanh(1/z) = ¼·log(|z + 1|²/|z − 1|²) + i·½·atan2(−2y, |z|² − 1); acoth 0 = iπ/2; 0 at ±1
acoth ξ ≔ ((ϕ ψ ↦ ((∧ (≐ ψ 0) (≐ (abs ϕ) 1)) (⁂ 0) ((θ ↦ ((∧ (≐ ψ 0) (lt_cx 1 (abs ϕ))) θ (cpxR_cx θ (sclR_cx (÷ 1 1100) (at2S_cx (⊠ 11100 ψ) (⊟ (𝒩 ξ) 1)))))) (sclR_cx (÷ 1 111010000) (lpS_cx (÷ (𝒩 (⊞ ξ 1)) (𝒩 (⊟ ξ 1)))))))) (ℜ ξ) (ℑ ξ))
acothᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ inverse hyperbolic cotangent of a lazy argument
acothᴿ ≔ (⟐ acoth)
asech ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ inverse hyperbolic secant acosh(1/z); 0 at z = 0 (pole)
asech ξ ≔ ((≐ ξ 0) (⁂ 0) (acosh (÷ 1 ξ)))
asechᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]   ⍝ inverse hyperbolic secant of a lazy argument
asechᴿ ≔ (⟐ asech)
acsch ∶ ℚ → ℝ   ⍝ inverse hyperbolic cosecant asinh(1/z); 0 at z = 0 (pole)
acsch ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
acsch ξ ≔ ((≐ ξ 0) (⁂ 0) (asinh (÷ 1 ξ)))
acschᴿ ∶ ℝ → ℝ   ⍝ inverse hyperbolic cosecant of a lazy argument
acschᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
acschᴿ ≔ (⟐ acsch)
⍝ ==== special functions
⍝ ---- Bernoulli numbers B₂ₖ from the tangent numbers Tₖ (integers; Brent–Harvey): start with Tₖ = (k − 1)!, then in round k = 2, 3, …
⍝ Tⱼ ← (j − k)·Tⱼ₋₁ + (j − k + 2)·Tⱼ for j = k, k + 1, … (Tⱼ₋₁ already updated); Tₖ is final after round k, and
⍝ B₂ₖ = (−1)^(k−1)·2k·Tₖ/(4ᵏ(4ᵏ − 1)).  The rows are infinite lazy lists of digit strings (row k: the values after round k).
tsc_cx ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇
tsc_cx κ ω ξ ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ ((ν ↦ (∷ ν (tsc_cx (⊞ᶻ κ (◀ 1)) ν ι))) (⊞ᶻ (⊠ᶻ κ ω) (⊠ᶻ (⊞ᶻ κ (◀ 1100)) θ)))) ⊥)
trows_cx ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇 → 𝔖 (𝔏 𝔇)
trows_cx ν ξ ≔ (∷ ξ (trows_cx (⊞ᶻ ν (◀ 1)) (⧺ (take′ ν ξ) (tsc_cx ⊥ ⊥ (drop′ ν ξ)))))
fl_cx ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔖 𝔇
fl_cx ν φ ≔ (∷ φ (fl_cx (⊞ᶻ ν (◀ 1)) (⊠ᶻ φ ν)))
tang_cx ∶ 𝔖 (𝔏 𝔇)
tang_cx ≔ (trows_cx (◀ 1) (fl_cx (◀ 1) (◀ 1)))
⍝ the stream B₂, B₄, B₆, … (canonical fractions; a global stream, so every element is computed once)
berns_cx ∶ 𝔖 ℚ
berns_cx ≔ (⫶ (κ ↦ ((υ ↦ (⊜ (÷ (⊠ (⊠ (^ 11101 (⊟ κ 1)) (⊠ 1100 κ)) (⊗ (hd (drop (⊟ κ 1) (hd (drop (⊟ κ 1) tang_cx)))) (◀ 1))) (⊠ υ (⊟ υ 1))))) (^ 111010000 κ))) (iterate (ν ↦ (⊞ ν 1)) 1))
⍝ B₂ₖ (k ≥ 1)
bern_cx ∶ ℕ → ℚ
bern_cx κ ≔ (hd (drop (⊟ κ 1) berns_cx))
⍝ ---- asymptotic series of log Γ and ψ.  For an exact w with Re w ≥ |Im w| (|arg w| ≤ π/4) the remainder of
⍝   log Γ(w) = (w − ½)·log w − w + ½·log 2π + Σₖ₌₁^(K−1) B₂ₖ/(2k(2k − 1)·w^(2k−1)) + R_K
⍝   ψ(w)     = log w − 1/(2w) − Σₖ₌₁^(K−1) B₂ₖ/(2k·w^(2k)) + R_K
⍝ is at most the first omitted term in modulus (Stieltjes' integral for the remainder, with |w²/(t² + w²)| ≤ 1 for t ≥ 0 when
